# The topmost certificate of the chain each host sent, recorded on 2026-09-29 16:57 UTC with
#     openssl s_client -connect <host>:443 -servername <host> -showcerts
# (385 hosts, 316 answered) and reduced the way ESP-IDF v5.3's esp_crt_verify_callback sees it:
# follow the sent certificates from the leaf to its issuer while one is there and its
# signature checks; the last one reached is the top, and the bundle is searched for the top's
# issuer. Hosts that send the same top share one entry.
#
# `needs-anchor` entries are every top that failed with cacert.pem alone (93 hosts); they pass
# with anchors.pem. `store` entries pass with cacert.pem alone. test_ca_store.py checks both,
# and fails when an anchor in software/wifi/ca_store/anchors.pem is needed by no entry here
# that has not expired. Record again when servers change their chains, and remove an entry
# when no host sends it.

